  "result": "Perfect! All 204 tests pass (193 original + 11 new). I've successfully added voucher support.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Added error code** to `src/errors.js`:\n   - `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: This invoice already has a voucher\n\n2. **Created `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`** in `src/invoices.js`:\n   - Validates invoice status is `'draft'` \u2192 NOT_DRAFT\n   - Checks for existing voucher \u2192 VOUCHER_EXISTS\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer \u2192 AMOUNT_INVALID\n   - Stores `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Never mutates original invoice\n\n3. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`**:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n   - `voucher`: Amount from `invoice.voucher?.amount` (0 if no voucher)\n   - `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped at 0)\n\n**Tests added (11 new):**\n- Applying voucher to draft invoice\n- Voucher correctly reduces total\n- Rejecting voucher on issued invoices (NOT_DRAFT)\n- Rejecting second voucher (VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n- Amount validation (negative, zero, fractional)\n- Input immutability\n- Voucher in invoiceTotals calculation\n- Zero voucher for invochers without vouchers\n- Total never goes below zero with large vouchers\n\n**Formula:**\n```\ntotal = (subtotal - discount + vat) - voucher\n```\n\nVoucher is a fixed amount that applies **after** VAT, reducing the final total (but never going negative).\n\nAll 204 tests pass, confirming complete voucher functionality with proper validation and immutability.",
